 meets barry  some iterations like the cw's flash  series  portray iris and berry as being friends  since childhood  in the television series barry was  essentially raised as a part of iris's  family  following the death of his mother who  was killed by the villainous eobard thon  no matter how they end up meeting  however barry and iris always seem to  end up together  and although they have their differences  they clearly love each other dearly  they were even engaged and eventually  married for a while in the comics  with iris finally learning that barry is  secretly the flash  about a year after they tied the knot  being in love with a superhero certainly  has its perks but it also inevitably  leads to great pain  too after all if you have an enemy who  has dedicated their entire life to  seeing you suffer  a non-superpowered loved one is  basically a flashing neon target  naturally with flash's nemesis reverse  flash looking to harm barry allen in  every possible timeline  it was only a matter of time before the  super villain tried to bring her down  too reverse flash isn't exactly one for  subtlety  but he was once able to find a way to  corner iris without sacrificing any of  his characteristic flair  in this story he finds barry's then wife  at a costume party  where he is cleverly disguised as  himself  iris meanwhile is dressed as batgirl a  character who has been attacked by more  than a few super villains herself  during the party reverse flash who is  then known as professor zoom  uses his speed powers to vibrate his  hand through iris's skull  scrambling her brain and killing her  instantly  though iris remains dead for a while in  barry's timeline  it's later revealed that she's actually  doing well elsewhere  in the meantime barry falls in love  again and zoom  true to form attempts to kill his next  fiance too  that's rude while iris is absent from  barry's life for quite some time  another iris exists further up the time  stream after yet another 