d vigilante  career as the hero known as  impulse as you might imagine  iris tends to feel deeply uncomfortable  living in the 20th century  being in an entirely new more primitive  time makes her uneasy to say the least  so she decides to go into hiding rather  than deal with the demands of 20th  century life  unfortunately it's hard to stay under  the radar when you hold the secrets of  the future  the history contained in her brain makes  her a massive target for villains hoping  to get one  over on their enemies when ira sticks  her neck out to help johnny quick  win a battle with the speed force  worshiping cult leader  savitar she ends up giving herself away  she is subsequently kidnapped by polaris  and abracadabra so that they might plot  world domination using her  insight when she manages to escape she  goes underground again  eventually publishing a history of the  flash from an undisclosed  location after becoming embroiled in a  case of mistaken identity  regarding wally west's supposed  illegitimate child  iris opts to come out of hiding and  spend more time with her family  iris's newfound family life is turned on  its head  by the flashpoint miniseries in this  massive line-wide event  barry allen realizes that he's woken up  in an alternate world  and is the only one who remembers life  as it's supposed to be  superman's place in the pantheon has  been taken up by cyborg  thomas wayne is not only not dead but  he's actually batman  meanwhile wonder woman and aquaman are  locked in a forever war  and the justice league doesn't even  exist in this reality iris west is  married to another reporter  though her nephew wally west still  exists he has nothing to do with the  speed force  and is eventually killed during the  events of the story in an attempt to set  the world right  barry and thomas wayne try to reawaken  his speed powers  so that he might fix the altered  timeline the first attempt goes poorly  to say the least and barry ends up  horribly 